Basic Extent Report Questions
	1. What is Extent Reports in Selenium?
		○ Extent Reports is a logging and reporting library used to generate detailed, interactive HTML reports for Selenium test executions.
	2. What are the key features of Extent Reports?
		○ Interactive HTML reports
		○ Logs with screenshots
		○ Test case status (PASS, FAIL, SKIP)
		○ Timestamped logs
		○ Integration with TestNG, JUnit, Cucumber, etc.
	3. How do you add Extent Reports to your Maven project?
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.aventstack</groupId>
    <artifactId>extentreports</artifactId>
    <version>5.0.9</version> <!-- Use latest -->
</dependency>
Usage and Implementation Questions
	1. How do you create and initialize an Extent Report in Selenium with Java?
ExtentReports extent = new ExtentReports();
ExtentSparkReporter spark = new ExtentSparkReporter("ExtentReport.html");
extent.attachReporter(spark);
	2. How do you create a test entry in the Extent Report?
ExtentTest test = extent.createTest("Login Test");
test.pass("Navigated to login page");
	3. How do you flush the report at the end of test execution?
extent.flush();
Intermediate/Scenario-Based Questions
	1. How do you log different test statuses in Extent Report?
test.pass("Test passed");
test.fail("Test failed");
test.skip("Test skipped");
	2. How do you attach screenshots in Extent Reports?
test.addScreenCaptureFromPath("screenshots/login_failed.png");
	3. How do you integrate Extent Reports with TestNG or JUnit?
		○ Use a TestNG listener (ITestListener) or a base class to initialize and flush Extent Reports in @BeforeSuite and @AfterSuite.
	4. How do you generate a report for each test suite or each test class?
	• Create separate Extent Test instances per test method or class.
	• Store the Extent Test in a ThreadLocal object for parallel execution.

Advanced/Best Practices Questions
	1. How do you use ThreadLocal for ExtentTest in parallel execution?
private static ThreadLocal<ExtentTest> extentTest = new ThreadLocal<>();
public static ExtentTest getTest() {
    return extentTest.get();
}
public static void setTest(ExtentTest test) {
    extentTest.set(test);
}
	1. How do you customize Extent Report (theme, title, name)?
spark.config().setTheme(Theme.DARK);
spark.config().setReportName("Automation Test Report");
spark.config().setDocumentTitle("Selenium Report");
	1. Can you log exception stack traces in Extent Reports?
try {
    // test code
} catch (Exception e) {
    test.fail(e);
}
	1. What is the difference between ExtentReports v3 and v5?
	• v5 (current) uses ExtentSparkReporter instead of ExtentHtmlReporter.
	• v5 supports more custom layouts and reporting capabilities.
Real-World Scenario Questions
	1. How do you create a report that includes pass/fail test counts, screenshots, and logs?
	• Use ExtentTest.log() for logs, addScreenCaptureFromPath() for screenshots, and let ExtentReports handle status counts automatically in the summary.
	2. How do you generate a separate report for every execution?
	• Append timestamp to the file name:
String timestamp = new SimpleDateFormat("yyyyMMddHHmmss").format(new Date());
ExtentSparkReporter spark = new ExtentSparkReporter("ExtentReport_" + timestamp + ".html");
